The `TarArchiveInputStream.getNextTarEntry()` method is responsible for retrieving the next `TarArchiveEntry` from the input stream in the `Tar` archive. Here is a snippet of the method:

```java
public TarArchiveEntry getNextTarEntry() throws IOException {
    if (hasHitEOF) {
        return null;
    }

    if (currEntry != null) {
        /* Skip will only go to the end of the current entry */
        skip(Long.MAX_VALUE);

        /* skip to the end of the last record */
        skipRecordPadding();
    }

    byte[] headerBuf = getRecord();

    if (headerBuf == null) {
        /* hit EOF */
        currEntry = null;
        return null;
    }

    try {
        currEntry = new TarArchiveEntry(headerBuf, encoding);
    } catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
        IOException ioe = new IOException("Error detected parsing the header");
        ioe.initCause(e);
        throw ioe;
    }

    entryOffset = 0;
    entrySize = currEntry.getSize();

    if (currEntry.isGNULongLinkEntry()) {
        byte[] longLinkData = getLongNameData();
        if (longLinkData == null) {
            // Handle case where long link data is missing
            return null;
        }
        currEntry.setLinkName(encoding.decode(longLinkData));
    }

    // Additional processing for GNULongNameEntry, Pax headers, and GNUSparse

    return currEntry;
}
```

In this method, when `headerBuf == null`, the method indicates that it has hit the EOF (End of File) and sets `currEntry` to `null` before returning `null`. This handling seems appropriate for detecting the end of the archive.

